:name: HawkHealth (STM32F767) — local dev
:description: Watch HawkHealth telemetry on USART3, using your locally built firmware.
#
# ZERO EDITS NEEDED — if you launch Renode FROM YOUR CLONE ROOT, e.g.:
#     cd <your-clone>            # the folder containing firmware/ platforms/ tests/
#     renode renode/hawkhealth-local.resc
# then the relative @paths below resolve to your just-built ELF and the board model.
# (If you launch Renode from somewhere else, either cd to the clone first, or use the
#  original renode/hawkhealth.resc with absolute paths.)
#
using sysbus
mach create "hawkhealth"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/hawkhealth_f767.repl
sysbus LoadELF @firmware/hawkhealth.elf
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart3
#
# Then, at the (hawkhealth) monitor prompt:  start
# Watch for:  call 300 -> temp 38.5 -> alert=HIGH ;  call 500 -> spo2 88.0 -> alert=CRITICAL
# Rebuilt the firmware? At the prompt:  Reset  then  sysbus LoadELF @firmware/hawkhealth.elf  then  start
